# M0.3b — MACE full-cell under `hybrid/overlay` with `dispersion/d3`.
#         Community-confirmed pattern (matsci #62930) but unproven in our stack.
#
# Geometry: bilayer_mos2.data from make_geometries.py — 24 atoms, 4 atom types.
# TYPE LAYOUT:
#   1 = Mo layer 1   2 = S layer 1
#   3 = Mo layer 2   4 = S layer 2
# Both coeff lines list a real element for every type — `dispersion/d3` requires
# it, and `pair_style mace` cannot take NULL anyway.
#
# NOTE: the dispersion/d3 argument order must match the *ACEsuit fork's* d3
# implementation, which is older than pinned mainline and may use the pre-rename
# damping tokens. Verify against the build's own docs, keep it identical to the
# form verified in M0.2 only if both builds agree, and record BOTH in
# documentation/milestone0.md — spec §1.2 makes d3_damping a canonical name
# precisely because the two builds can disagree.
#
# Run:  $PREFIX/lammps-mace/build/lmp -k on g 1 -sf kk -in m0_3b_mace_overlay_d3.in
#
# PASS: 20 steps complete, finite energy/forces, D3 contribution non-zero
#       (E_pair differs from M0.3 by the dispersion energy).

units metal
atom_style atomic
read_data bilayer_mos2.data
pair_style hybrid/overlay mace no_domain_decomposition dispersion/d3 bj pbe 16.0 8.0
pair_coeff * * mace mace.model-lammps.pt Mo S Mo S
pair_coeff * * dispersion/d3 Mo S Mo S
# Masses are also in the data file; repeated here so the deck is self-contained.
mass 1 95.95   # Mo
mass 2 32.06   # S
mass 3 95.95   # Mo
mass 4 32.06   # S
thermo 1
run 0
fix nve all nve
run 20
